# What tests/vt.sh's boot starts once the drivers are running: the
# demo's /etc/system with two terminals, whatever the demo starts after
# its first. The serial shell, which boot waits for; wm, the compositor;
# and two vts, pids 17 and 18, each a Terminal window with a tab, whose
# relay registers it as vt1 or vt2, whichever is free first, and whose
# shell, sh vt1 or sh vt2, the window's vt starts; a window closes when
# its last tab's shell exits. make vt-initramfs puts this over the
# demo's own.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/wm
start /Applications/Terminal.app/vt
start /Applications/Terminal.app/vt
